{"content": "Here is the bash command to find files larger than 100MB under the `/var` directory:\n\n```bash\nsudo find /var -type f -size +100M -exec ls -lh {} \\;\n```\n\n### Explanation of Flags and Options\n\n*   **`sudo`**: The `/var` directory often contains system files owned by root. Running with `sudo` ensures you have permission to access and list all files, not just those owned by your current user.\n*   **`find`**: The standard utility for searching files in a directory hierarchy.\n*   **`/var`**: The starting directory for the search.\n*   **`-type f`**: Restricts the search to **regular files** only. This excludes directories, symbolic links, sockets, etc.\n*   **`-size +100M`**: Filters files based on size.\n    *   `+` means \"greater than\".\n    *   `100M` specifies the size threshold (100 Megabytes).\n    *   *Note: You can also use `k` for kilobytes or `G` for gigabytes.*\n*   **`-exec", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.5656779192550907, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.5656779192550907}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -1.1620219133957157}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -2.633413591252161}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -3.2588980578048954}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -5.4785826586349735}, {"token": "`", "logprob": -6.280592241154505}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -6.321777620182825}, {"token": "Use", "logprob": -8.646456041203333}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.712400712834192}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -8.94923619257052}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -9.022405900822474}, {"token": "B", "logprob": -9.508741655217005}, {"token": "Command", "logprob": -10.278692521916224}, {"token": "Run", "logprob": -10.365501680241419}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -10.822256364689661}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -10.956542291508509}, {"token": "to", "logprob": -10.992812433110071}, {"token": "One", "logprob": -11.000838556156946}, {"token": "`,", "logprob": -11.122685708866907}, {"token": "First", "logprob": -11.16314534